<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Policyholder questions</nav><p class="tag">Answers by topic</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Questions from Rhode Island Owners</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers about the appraisal process, costs, timing and how Rhode Island rules fit in, grouped by topic.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn glass" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Topics"><p class="note-t">Jump to a topic</p><ul><li><a href="#q-0">The basics</a></li><li><a href="#q-1">When appraisal fits</a></li><li><a href="#q-2">Costs &amp; timing</a></li><li><a href="#q-3">Rhode Island specifics</a></li><li><a href="#q-4">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="q-0">The basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process written into most property policies for settling disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and any two of the three can sign a binding award on the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>What does a Rhode Island insurance appraiser do?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>As your appointed appraiser, we inspect, build an independent line-item valuation, work through the differences with the carrier’s appraiser and, if needed, present unresolved items to the umpire.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as mediation?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Mediation is voluntary and non-binding unless you sign a settlement. An appraisal award on the amount of loss is generally binding.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They’re similar, but appraisal is narrower. It decides the amount of loss, not legal questions like coverage.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="q-1">When appraisal fits</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>When should I consider appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When coverage is accepted, you have the carrier’s itemized estimate and a credible estimate of your own, and the gap between them is meaningful.</p></div></details><details><summary>When is appraisal the wrong tool?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When the claim was denied, when the dispute is about coverage or causation, when the gap is too small to justify fees, or when a deadline is close and you need legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can the insurer demand appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Most policies let either side invoke it.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal handle wind versus flood questions?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal under your homeowner policy values the covered loss. Whether damage was caused by wind or flood is usually a causation and coverage question outside appraisal.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="q-2">Costs &amp; timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What does appraisal cost?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Each side pays its own appraiser, and the umpire’s fee is usually split. Fee arrangements vary; ask for one in writing.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A few weeks for a straightforward residential claim once appraisers are named. Complex or commercial claims can take several months.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is your first conversation free?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal is likely to help.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="q-3">Rhode Island specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance in Rhode Island?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Rhode Island Department of Business Regulation, through its Insurance Division. It handles consumer complaints and licenses insurers, agents and adjusters.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the Rhode Island FAIR Plan?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A property insurer of last resort for owners who can’t find coverage in the regular market, often near the coast. FAIR Plan policies have their own terms, including how disputes over the amount of loss are handled.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do Rhode Island policies have hurricane deductibles?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many do. They’re usually a percentage of dwelling coverage and apply when the storm meets the policy’s trigger. Check your declarations page.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Rhode Island have a bad-faith law?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Rhode Island has a statute allowing an insured to bring a claim against an insurer for bad-faith refusal to pay or settle. Whether it applies is a legal question for a Rhode Island attorney; appraisal doesn’t decide it.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you serve the whole state?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, all 39 cities and towns across Rhode Island’s five counties, including Block Island by arrangement.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="q-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Neither. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We don’t give legal advice or negotiate claims outside the appraisal process.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you guarantee a result?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. No honest appraiser can. We can promise a thorough, documented valuation.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send first?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page and policy, the carrier’s full estimate, any contractor estimate, photos and the carrier’s letters.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through</h2><p>A free first conversation. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-phone" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Learn</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/the-appraisal-sequence/">The appraisal sequence<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/policyholder-questions/" aria-current="page">Policyholder questions<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-wordbook/">Claim wordbook<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-notebook/">Claim notebook<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></aside></div><section class="strip"><div class="wrap strip-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We’re happy to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn ink" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink-line" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
